"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[37405],{37405:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/the-source-of-happiness.png\\"\\n          title=\\"The Origin of Happiness\\"\\n          author=\\"Eun-kook Suh\\"\\n          publisher=\\"21st Century Books\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2024-05-22\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9791171175864\\"\\n          rating=4\\n          tags=\\"humanities\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nHumans do not live to be happy, but are just designed to feel happiness \\nto survive.  \\nHappiness is a <mark>survival tool</mark>, not a purpose.\\n<br>\\nActually, it\'s a fact I knew but wanted to ignore.  \\nThe means and the purpose have been swapped.\\nIt\'s a slightly uncomfortable truth I learned through ```The Selfish Gene```.\\n<br>\\nIt was interesting that there are separate genetic temperaments that have a huge impact on happiness.  \\nExtroverted people feel ```happiness``` in the process of meeting and hanging out with people itself, and that this is a <mark>social animal</mark> and this is essential for survival, it was perhaps natural.  \\n<br>\\nI agree that happiness is about <mark>frequency</mark>, not <mark>intensity</mark>.  \\nHumans quickly get used to any positive event and happiness is quickly reset.  \\nThis is also designed for survival.\\n<br>\\nSmall but certain happiness (So-hwak-haeng) is actually not small, but certain happiness.  \\n"}')}}]);